1
00:00:02,020 --> 00:00:07,940
Tidepath Family Alliance: a made-up Miami nonprofit. 7 staff roles, 1 operator, Alex. Outsiders use a public portal. Staff work in Roomcord, and each room has an AI agent for one job.

2
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:10,473
Roomcord is the private workspace where the staff work.

3
00:00:10,553 --> 00:00:14,473
Tidepath works in 9 rooms. Each room has one job and one AI agent.

4
00:00:14,553 --> 00:00:18,473
Kids and families: Programs, Volunteers, Workshop requests, Counseling.

5
00:00:18,553 --> 00:00:21,973
Money: Fundraising, and Grants and finance.

6
00:00:22,053 --> 00:00:25,973
Director desk routes work. People CRM holds every person's record.

7
00:00:26,053 --> 00:00:28,973
P5. Volunteer hours get lost, and urgent needs wait for days.

8
00:00:29,053 --> 00:00:31,507
The Tidepath portal is a public website with no login.

9
00:00:31,587 --> 00:00:35,673
Maria, a volunteer mentor, opens the check-in form in Spanish.

10
00:00:35,753 --> 00:00:40,939
She logs 1 hour with Kevin and marks an urgent need: a laptop.

11
00:00:41,019 --> 00:00:43,973
She taps Send. No login, no app to install.

12
00:00:44,053 --> 00:00:46,506
Now we switch to Roomcord, where the staff work.

13
00:00:46,586 --> 00:00:50,506
Maria's check-in arrives in the Volunteers room as a portal message.

14
00:00:50,586 --> 00:00:55,506
The agent logs the hour once and flags the laptop need as urgent.

15
00:00:55,586 --> 00:00:58,706
Alex asks the Director agent to send the need to the Programs room.

16
00:00:58,786 --> 00:01:02,706
The Director agent posts the need in Programs and mentoring.

17
00:01:02,786 --> 00:01:06,206
In the room list, Programs and mentoring now shows a new message.

18
00:01:06,286 --> 00:01:08,006
Alex opens the Programs and mentoring room.

19
00:01:08,086 --> 00:01:11,506
The urgent need is here the same day, with a mention for Alex.

20
00:01:11,586 --> 00:01:14,506
P1. Kids at risk get missed until it is too late.

21
00:01:14,586 --> 00:01:17,239
Alex asks the Programs agent: who needs a call this week?

22
00:01:17,319 --> 00:01:19,406
The agent checks attendance and mentor meetings in the CRM.

23
00:01:19,486 --> 00:01:23,906
Kevin and Jaylen missed sessions. They need a call this week.

24
00:01:23,986 --> 00:01:26,839
Alex asks for a follow-up message to Kevin's mother, in Spanish.

25
00:01:26,919 --> 00:01:29,239
The agent writes the draft.

26
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:34,239
The reply says DRAFT, not sent. A person approves before anything is sent.

27
00:01:34,319 --> 00:01:36,773
The People CRM app runs inside the Roomcord room 'People CRM'.

28
00:01:36,853 --> 00:01:39,339
In the People CRM room, Alex opens the People CRM tab.

29
00:01:39,419 --> 00:01:42,939
One list of 67 people: kids, parents, mentors, volunteers and donors.

30
00:01:43,019 --> 00:01:46,539
Duplicates: records that may be the same person.

31
00:01:46,619 --> 00:01:49,939
Rosa Delgado is in the CRM twice: same phone, same address.

32
00:01:50,019 --> 00:01:52,739
Alex clicks Approve merge.

33
00:01:52,819 --> 00:01:57,773
The record keeps who approved it, the time, and the history.

34
00:01:57,853 --> 00:02:01,373
This week: the mentoring kids at risk, each with a draft follow-up.

35
00:02:01,453 --> 00:02:05,173
Alex approves Kevin's follow-up.

36
00:02:05,253 --> 00:02:10,106
Status: approved by Alex, with the time. The owner now calls the parent.

37
00:02:10,186 --> 00:02:12,839
Q3 report: the numbers that funders ask for.

38
00:02:12,919 --> 00:02:16,339
All totals reconcile with the source rows.

39
00:02:16,419 --> 00:02:19,839
Each total is counted again from the raw rows, and every check matches.

40
00:02:19,919 --> 00:02:22,839
P2. Regular donors stop giving, and nobody notices.

41
00:02:22,919 --> 00:02:24,439
Back in Roomcord, in the Fundraising room.

42
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:27,939
Alex asks the Fundraising agent which regular donors are late.

43
00:02:28,019 --> 00:02:29,306
The agent checks each donor's giving schedule.

44
00:02:29,386 --> 00:02:34,806
Two donors are late: a monthly gift by 35 days, a 90-day gift by 31 days.

45
00:02:34,886 --> 00:02:37,806
P3. Schools wait days for answers about workshops.

46
00:02:37,886 --> 00:02:40,339
Back to the public portal, on a phone.

47
00:02:40,419 --> 00:02:48,939
A school counselor requests a safety workshop in Spanish.

48
00:02:49,019 --> 00:02:51,773
She sends it. She does not need an account.

49
00:02:51,853 --> 00:02:53,373
Back in Roomcord, in the Workshop requests room.

50
00:02:53,453 --> 00:02:56,873
The request arrives in the Workshop requests room.

51
00:02:56,953 --> 00:03:02,373
The agent asks every missing question in one reply and opens request W002.

52
00:03:02,453 --> 00:03:04,906
Later, the school uses the portal again.

53
00:03:04,986 --> 00:03:12,939
Later, the school approves slides version 2 on the portal.

54
00:03:13,019 --> 00:03:14,539
Back in Roomcord.

55
00:03:14,619 --> 00:03:17,539
The approval arrives in the room.

56
00:03:17,619 --> 00:03:22,039
The tracker records school approved v2, and who approved it.

57
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:25,039
P4. Counseling notes are private, but funders need numbers.

58
00:03:25,119 --> 00:03:26,639
Back in Roomcord, in the restricted Counseling room.

59
00:03:26,719 --> 00:03:30,139
Alex asks what exactly goes to the funder from a sample note.

60
00:03:30,219 --> 00:03:34,139
WILL BE SENT: only service facts, like date, minutes, ZIP and age band.

61
00:03:34,219 --> 00:03:38,639
STAYS INSIDE: names, the narrative and risk flags. Nothing else leaves.

62
00:03:38,719 --> 00:03:41,639
P6. Grant spending is hard to track against the funder rules.

63
00:03:41,719 --> 00:03:43,239
Back in Roomcord, in the Grants and finance room.

64
00:03:43,319 --> 00:03:46,739
Alex asks how much is left per category in the county grant.

65
00:03:46,819 --> 00:03:48,106
The agent reads the grant budget and the spending.

66
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:53,106
Emergency aid has $800 left. No category is over 90%.

67
00:03:53,186 --> 00:03:55,639
Source code, open on GitHub.

68
00:03:55,719 --> 00:03:59,639
One repository holds every agent, skill, the portal and the CRM app.

69
00:03:59,719 --> 00:04:04,639
Each agent = a flavor: role + rules + skills.

70
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:09,173
Every detail entered once. Urgent needs reach staff the same day. Reports in minutes. A human approves everything.

